  the thing worth confirming rather than assuming: nothing in this repo binds the listener to localhost
  ([38;5;153mapp.listen(process.env.PORT || 3000)[39m binds all interfaces), so whether it's actually unreachable from outside depends
  on deployment, not on the code.

  Alternatives that unblock the dashboard team without opening the route:

  1. [1mService token[0m — accept a shared secret header in [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m alongside the session cookie. A few lines, keeps the
     route closed to everyone else.
  2. [1mGive the script a session[0m — it logs in once and reuses the cookie. No server change at all.
  3. [1mBind to localhost / trust a network boundary[0m — only if the deployment genuinely guarantees it, and still worth
     making explicit in code.

